From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] objc-config: let the build set OBJC_USE_ROSETTA

OBJC_USE_ROSETTA turns on the Rosetta hooks in objc-cache.mm (the
translated-process check and the cache-flush trap), which need Apple's
unpublished <Rosetta/Rosetta.h> and <Rosetta/Traps.h> and libRosetta. It is
derived from the target OS alone. NeoDarwin runs arm64 code only and has no
Rosetta, so its build defines OBJC_USE_ROSETTA=0; the derivation stays the
default for any build that doesn't. With it off the runtime behaves as it
does on Apple's platforms without Rosetta (the simulators, visionOS).

Rebase-risk: low (an #ifndef around the existing definition).
---
diff --git a/runtime/objc-config.h b/runtime/objc-config.h
--- a/runtime/objc-config.h
+++ b/runtime/objc-config.h
@@ -367,11 +367,14 @@
 // Whether to use Rosetta APIs. macOS and iOS use it, but not simulators or
 // other platforms. visionOS sets TARGET_OS_IOS in the internal SDK so we need
 // to explicitly exclude that
+// NeoDarwin: a build may set it (a system without Rosetta sets it to 0).
+#ifndef OBJC_USE_ROSETTA
 #if   (TARGET_OS_OSX || TARGET_OS_IOS) && !TARGET_OS_VISION && !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR
 #define OBJC_USE_ROSETTA 1
 #else
 #define OBJC_USE_ROSETTA 0
 #endif
+#endif
 
 
 #endif
